---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DATA_VERSION, LAST_REVIEWED } from '@/data/us/meta';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology | Starbucks Nutrition Calculator"
  description="How this independent Starbucks nutrition calculator sources data, calculates customizations, and where its data is incomplete."
  path="/methodology/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p class="section__eyebrow">Methodology</p>
        <h1>Data &amp; methodology</h1>
        <p>Dataset version <strong>{DATA_VERSION}</strong>, last reviewed <strong>{LAST_REVIEWED}</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        This is an independent informational tool and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Starbucks Corporation. Product names are used only to
        identify the drinks this tool calculates nutrition for.
      </p>

      <h2>U.S. data scope</h2>
      <p>This tool is U.S.-focused only. It does not mix U.S. figures with Ireland, UK, EU, Canada or other regional Starbucks nutrition data.</p>

      <h2>How figures were compiled</h2>
      <p>
        The nutrition figures in this dataset were compiled from publicly available Starbucks nutrition data via third-party nutrition trackers and aggregator
        sites, because the environment used to assemble this dataset could not reach starbucks.com directly at compile time. Every drink and size record carries
        a <code>sourceUrl</code> pointing to the specific Starbucks nutrition page it should be checked against, and a <code>status</code> field of <code
          >needs-review</code
        > rather than <code>verified</code> until that check happens. No figure in this dataset has been marked <code>verified</code> without someone confirming it
        against starbucks.com directly.
      </p>

      <h2>Customization methodology</h2>
      <p>
        Every drink defines which sizes, milks and add-ins it actually supports; the calculator will not let you select or calculate an unsupported combination.
        Where a customization has a verified nutrition effect (for example, one espresso shot, which is consistently reported as about 5 calories and 75mg of
        caffeine), that effect is applied deterministically. Where it does not &mdash; most visibly, per-pump syrup and sauce nutrition &mdash; the calculator
        says &ldquo;ingredient-level calculation unavailable for this customization&rdquo; rather than invent a number.
      </p>

      <h2>Caffeine methodology</h2>
      <p>
        Caffeine figures come from the same per-drink sources as other nutrition fields, and may be approximate where the source data itself identifies them as
        approximate.
      </p>

      <h2>Allergen limitations</h2>
      <p>
        Allergen information reflects the primary allergens commonly associated with an ingredient (for example, milk or tree nuts). It is not a substitute for
        current official Starbucks allergen information and does not account for cross-contact in-store. Never treat an item as &ldquo;safe&rdquo; for an
        allergy based on this tool.
      </p>

      <h2>Update process</h2>
      <p>
        Data updates are tracked with a <code>dataVersion</code> and a <code>lastReviewed</code> date per record, and summarized in the <a href="/changelog/"
          >changelog</a
        >. Records are never silently overwritten with unreviewed guesses.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Only a curated set of drinks is covered so far; coverage will grow over time.</li>
        <li>Milk-substitution and syrup/sauce pump-level nutrition deltas are not yet verified for most drinks.</li>
        <li>Food items and seasonal drinks are not yet in the dataset.</li>
        <li>Figures reflect standard recipes; in-store preparation can vary.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
